00:09:46.570 --> 00:09:50.950
Stacy wrote in, Does a fetus have a right
to get child support?

00:09:50.950 --> 00:09:52.390
Hi.

00:09:52.390 --> 00:09:57.279
If life begins at conception, shouldn't child
support start at conception?

00:09:57.279 --> 00:09:58.600
Yours, Stacey.

00:09:58.600 --> 00:10:02.510
I've brought this up many times before.

00:10:02.510 --> 00:10:09.440
The issue about personhood at conception raises
really important questions.

00:10:09.440 --> 00:10:16.120
If a fetus is a citizen, if a citizen if a
fetus is a person at conception, then it is

00:10:16.120 --> 00:10:17.120
a citizen.

00:10:17.120 --> 00:10:18.120
Right?

00:10:18.120 --> 00:10:20.420
I mean, it should be able to be made a citizen.

00:10:20.420 --> 00:10:26.670
And even if it's the fetus of an undocumented
immigrant, they should be able to get citizenship

00:10:26.670 --> 00:10:31.100
after conception, because if it's a person,
people get citizenship.

00:10:31.100 --> 00:10:37.700
If it is a person at conception, then presumably
it would be entitled to child support as well.

00:10:37.700 --> 00:10:44.170
I mean, listen, good luck actually having
rational conversations about these things

00:10:44.170 --> 00:10:45.760
with the anti-choice movement.

00:10:45.760 --> 00:10:51.690
But of course, Stacey brings up a good point,
which is it's less about when do we say life

00:10:51.690 --> 00:10:53.810
has started?

00:10:53.810 --> 00:10:57.800
Forms of life exist in so many places and
in so many ways.

00:10:57.800 --> 00:11:02.770
And a fetus is less about whether it qualifies
as, quote, life.

00:11:02.770 --> 00:11:07.910
But what is a person and what are the rights
that come with personhood?

00:11:07.910 --> 00:11:12.620
Because the anti-choice movement wanted to
talk a lot about specific rights that they

00:11:12.620 --> 00:11:20.070
believe a fetus should have, but not about
many of the others that people, persons also

00:11:20.070 --> 00:11:21.070
get.

00:11:21.070 --> 00:11:22.600
And it's an age old hypocrisy.

00:11:22.600 --> 00:11:25.950
As long as Roe v Wade has been around, all
of these arguments have been around.

00:11:25.950 --> 00:11:30.950
And sadly, they very often become philosophical
black holes and you don't get anywhere with

00:11:30.950 --> 00:11:31.950
them.

00:11:31.950 --> 00:11:33.490
But an important question.

